  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-10-23T16:57:28.162Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If playspace is to be removed, please allow a feature to replace playspace mover. Often in worlds when I go prone in VR I am hovering a foot above the ground and not at ground level which takes away from the VR immersion. This can be a burden for players like me who greatly love to sleep in VR (practically every night), hovering a foot off the ground makes sleeping extremely awkward. If I could offer a recommendation, it would be great to have the ability to have an internal playspace feature where players can raise and lower their player space. I’ve had so many instances where we needed this feature. For example, In murder mysteries, we had items drop under the map and could only retrieve it with playspace mover. Another instance is where a player had thrown the weapon on a ledge in Murder 3 which was only possible to grab with playspace mover. \n\n Now, although I’m greatly advocating for this feature, I am sure players will exploit it. I believe unethical users will use this feature because of the simplicity of how accessible it is if it were to be added as a regular feature in the game. Therefore, it would probably be a better idea for users above a certain rank to unlock and gain access to this feature or perhaps allow it to be unlocked if VRChat has detected VR or full body integration from a user. \n\nIn conclusion, I believe having a feature like playspace mover built within VRChat will give players the freedom to choose how they want to play and enjoy VRChat.",
